{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794421184,"nonce":"fCUfYwtNrxd5xyefJGsnx4pTPlA=","message":"The library `hxn new` makes is now `examples/greeter`, read from there by the command, and `examples/` holds two more: `picture` (a lent function, bytes out, an object passed to another) and `primes` (a future awaited and continued, a stream). They are workspace members and depend on hxn by path, so `hxn run` works in place from a checkout. `tests/examples/run.sh hl|cpp` runs each and compares the last lines printed with its `expected.txt`; a unit test in hxn-gen holds each committed manifest to its source.\n\nRun on Ash (hybrid, jit, interp, five times each from the built main.hl), stock HashLink on the NUC, and hxcpp on macOS.\n\nOpen: the examples run on hl and cpp only, since the command has no wasm or Emscripten target yet. Nothing shows shared values, atomics, signals or a weighed interface outside the fixture.","files":null}]}